  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Cult Ambush" id="3db3-80e4-899c-debf" hidden="false">
      <description>If your Army Faction is GENESTEALER CULTS, you gain 6/10/14 Resurgence points (Incursion/Strike Force/Onslaught).
-&gt; Each time a friendly unit is destroyed, if every model in that unit (excluding CHARACTER models) has the Cult Ambush ability, you may use this ability:
  -&gt; Spend the Resurgence points the cost table gives for the datasheet and Starting Strength of that unit (Aberrants: 4 for 5 models, 8 for 10 models; Acolyte Hybrids with Autopistols, Acolyte Hybrids with Hand Flamers or Hybrid Metamorphs: 2 for 5 models, 4 for 10 models; Atalan Jackals: 2 for 5 models, 6 for 10 models; Neophyte Hybrids: 3 for 10 models, 6 for 20 models; Purestrain Genestealers: 2 for 5 models, 6 for 10 models).
  -&gt; Add a new unit identical to that unit (excluding CHARACTER models) to your army in Cult Ambush, at its Starting Strength and with all of its wounds remaining, with its [ONE SHOT] weapons counted as not having been shot.
  -&gt; Place a cult ambush marker (32mm) more than 9" horizontally away from all enemy units.
If your Army Faction is GENESTEALER CULTS:
  -&gt; Friendly units that are in Cult Ambush cannot be targeted with the Rapid Ingress Stratagem.
  -&gt; Friendly units that are in Cult Ambush are not destroyed for still being in Strategic Reserves at the end of the third battle round.
-&gt; Each time an enemy model ends a move (the triggering model must not have AIRCRAFT): if your Army Faction is GENESTEALER CULTS, while the triggering model is within 8" of a cult ambush marker, remove that cult ambush marker from the battlefield.
-&gt; At the end of your opponent's Movement phase, you may use this ability: if your Army Faction is GENESTEALER CULTS, select any number of friendly units that are in Cult Ambush (at most the number of your cult ambush markers on the battlefield): that unit can make an Ingress move; that unit can be set up on the battlefield using a Cult Ambush marker, wholly within 3" of that marker, even in the first battle round.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
